{#- testing/remote_harness/templates/lme-controller-seed.sh.j2 -- renders the managed-controller seed.
    Inputs (all declarations, never extra-vars of desired state):
      lme_seed_bs   = profile remote_harness.controller.bootstrap
      lme_seed_ctl  = profile remote_harness.controller
      lme_seed_lock = the file named by remote_harness.controller.lock_file_rel
      lme_seed_dispatch = profile remote_harness.controller.entry_generation.dispatch (r2i: the seed's entry-dispatch
                      metadata, an EXPLICIT declared input; route fields + the C1-derived entries / roster_rel /
                      source_members_rel -- output paths only, never digests, so regeneration does not re-key the seed)
                      r2j: source_members_rel is WITHDRAWN from dispatch; the seed's source admission reads
                      lme_seed_bs.source_admission (members_rel, importers, bootstrap_input, git edition grammar) --
                      the same bound bootstrap node admit_loader_source.yml consumes (no new template input).
    Rendered by package.yml (ansible.builtin.template) into <bundle>/lme-controller-seed.sh, a local build output
    that is never committed; verify_toolchain_receipt.yml re-renders it inline (lookup template) to derive the
    expected seed sha256 and generation id. -#}
{%- import 'macros/controller_seed.j2' as m -%}
{#- r2n OD-01 (a-prime) as realized by L-11 (codex-tick498 R2N-L11-NONROLE-REUSE): the packaged tools record is the
    loader-projected controller.bootstrap.packaged_tools (registry policy_projections.seed_packaged_tools: exactly the
    source_admission.tool_roles roles, {<tool_fields.path>, <tool_fields.sha256>} each), serialized here and passed to
    m.seed as _sa_tools_json. No template reads an executable identity, so all four artifacts keep not_embedded_fields
    [identity] under the full proof; the selected identities reach the seed reuse key through the projected leaves. It is
    DATA in the admitted seed bytes; admit_loader_source.yml binds the run-time selection and the executable's digest to
    it before first use. -#}
{%- set _sa_tools_json = lme_seed_bs.packaged_tools | tojson -%}
{#- brr-follow OD-BRR-07 (codex-tick543): lme_seed_dispatch is a template input ONLY under source_admission.dispatch_admission
    mode generation (the seed's own selector); otherwise it is never read and m.seed receives none, which entry_verify
    never dereferences outside generation (no empty dispatch view). -#}
{{ m.seed(lme_seed_bs, lme_seed_ctl, lme_seed_lock, (lme_seed_dispatch if lme_seed_bs.source_admission.dispatch_admission.mode == lme_seed_bs.source_admission.dispatch_modes.generation else none), _sa_tools_json) }}
